    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 176,
        "text": "Hi, everyone. Thanks for coming. As you know, the company has a new energy rule. We must cut electricity use by 20 percent this month. I know it's hard, but we can do it.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "1843b22e9767403eb39fd46f78e8eef468b296727b5e7410cc13596fffafdea9",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "tom",
        "speaker": "Tom",
        "sourceStart": 182,
        "sourceEnd": 265,
        "text": "Sorry, Maya, can I ask something? Why this month? Is it because of the hot weather?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "1ced33048975d8b922728e4234d7cc78c008d05194580d5406df136c289f3474",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 272,
        "sourceEnd": 445,
        "text": "Good question. The main reason is that our energy costs went up a lot last year. So the company wants to save money. Also, the government may give a reward to green offices.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "a7c848629b720674d0656633aadf93e8173377cd7f322857ab01dcab79480425",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "tom",
        "speaker": "Tom",
        "sourceStart": 451,
        "sourceEnd": 512,
        "text": "I see. So if we use less power, we might get some money back?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "33377a973e1e27397352aa529badd68eb1be2902fb6a5120fc4d1c00c953f2e7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 519,
        "sourceEnd": 602,
        "text": "Exactly. But we don't have to do anything dangerous. We can still work comfortably.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "4d6eaae8fd6d80303234a07d7a013289a254696bdde9233f0bb15194b10679fe",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "lisa",
        "speaker": "Lisa",
        "sourceStart": 609,
        "sourceEnd": 712,
        "text": "I have an idea. We could turn off the lights near the windows. The sun is very bright in the afternoon.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "21e9b686fec3c2a3f93581f06161509a1367f7c495d071e28609f20f6ab09afd",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 719,
        "sourceEnd": 854,
        "text": "That's a great idea, Lisa. We can do that. But please don't turn off the lights in the hallway. It's dark there, and people might fall.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "241272c333049899a9cc1a1b0f9646b0ce036487fb82349bc5686a6133adebd6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "tom",
        "speaker": "Tom",
        "sourceStart": 860,
        "sourceEnd": 912,
        "text": "What about the air conditioning? Can we turn it off?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "a272a79e7db6ff535cbb67d819ba3cd203c59f1a4d3c42b0b4d51adde1b4ce9f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 919,
        "sourceEnd": 1040,
        "text": "Hmm, we may not turn it off completely. It's very hot today. But we can set it to 26 degrees. That saves a lot of energy.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "c14af92b1f21c155d3437312d74af788b3a80ed5642afcbd25aaea7da90e5f2b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "tom",
        "speaker": "Tom",
        "sourceStart": 1046,
        "sourceEnd": 1110,
        "text": "OK. And the printers? They use power when we are not using them.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "2b329df3660f21e8622ddadb9d83aa9330484df6dc177c7298bcae92e457dae4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1117,
        "sourceEnd": 1266,
        "text": "Yes, they do. So we should turn them off at night. But wait—I mean, we can turn them off at night, but not during the day. Some people need to print.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "9a0607d9fcbae07e3e3334d9d6b10ad3e6f713c62beb80fed97e5b10bb708645",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "lisa",
        "speaker": "Lisa",
        "sourceStart": 1273,
        "sourceEnd": 1319,
        "text": "What about the coffee machine? It's always on.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "81874300417d31b2066dcbf56b8805c2017a103320253908410703eccb4a5a36",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1326,
        "sourceEnd": 1486,
        "text": "Good point. The coffee machine can stay on during work hours. But we might turn it off after 6 p.m. Actually, let's turn it off after 6. It's not a big problem.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "ceb7c97e44aacad2f60949a9110a8997f00b618207a9d9a4eb6244b0e9944f4b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "tom",
        "speaker": "Tom",
        "sourceStart": 1492,
        "sourceEnd": 1607,
        "text": "So, to sum up: lights off near windows, AC at 26, printers off at night, coffee machine off after 6. Is that right?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "bd2105aecd23c387dfe45db7db17cb7374da1a639b0e96a65aef81d2cb30dc86",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1614,
        "sourceEnd": 1757,
        "text": "Yes, that's right. And one more thing: if we save energy, the company may give us a small bonus. But I'm not sure yet. It's only a possibility.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "bbadfa14a2c7c8d8737aae616af8f88040e205c3870329e3f5b9a242b733bdb3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "lisa",
        "speaker": "Lisa",
        "sourceStart": 1764,
        "sourceEnd": 1824,
        "text": "Even if we don't get a bonus, it's good for the environment.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "3016beeba5f942add967fcf1520b11f1f5c01a0045bfcd95713589556ebc9e08",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1831,
        "sourceEnd": 1914,
        "text": "True. Although it's a small change, it can make a big difference. Thanks, everyone.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "fa1a9a768609df9b59aedebca0e377ecc6ba307e4456f9b4779374fa5613e878",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
